IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `caa-types`

-- The Convention, Chapter IV (combined carriage, Article 31) and Chapter V (general and final
-- provisions, Articles 32 to 41), and the Additional Protocol.
-- Source: source/CAA1988.txt lines 692 to 821 (First Schedule), 1269 to 1391 (Second Schedule)
-- and 1913 to 2041 (Third Schedule).  Articles 30A, 34 and 35 are dealt with where they
-- belong: 30A is inert (caa-convention-liability.l4), 34 is in caa-convention-scope.l4.

§ `Chapter IV -- Combined carriage`

§§ `Article 31`

-- 31(1): in combined carriage partly by air and partly by another mode, the Convention
-- applies only to the carriage by air, provided that falls within Article 1.  31(2): the
-- parties may insert in the document of air carriage conditions relating to other modes,
-- provided the Convention is observed as regards the carriage by air.

@ref "Convention, Article 31(1)"
GIVEN k IS A `Combined Carriage Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Convention applies to the part of the carriage performed by air` IF
        k's `the carriage is performed partly by air and partly by another mode of carriage`
    AND k's `the carriage by air falls within the terms of Article 1`

@ref "Convention, Article 31(2)"
GIVEN k IS A `Combined Carriage Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the parties may insert conditions relating to the other mode of carriage` IF
        k's `the carriage is performed partly by air and partly by another mode of carriage`
    AND k's `the parties inserted in the document of air carriage conditions relating to another mode of carriage`
    AND k's `the provisions of the Convention are observed as regards the carriage by air`

§ `Chapter V -- General and final provisions`

§§ `Article 32. Clauses infringing the Convention`

-- 32: any clause and special agreement entered into before the damage occurred by which the
-- parties purport to infringe the Convention, whether by deciding the law to be applied or by
-- altering the rules as to jurisdiction, is null and void.  For cargo, arbitration clauses
-- are allowed, subject to the Convention, if the arbitration is to take place within one of
-- the jurisdictions referred to in Article 28(1).

@ref "Convention, Article 32"
GIVEN k IS A `Clause Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an arbitration clause is allowed by Article 32` IF
        k's `the clause is an arbitration clause`
    AND k's `the carriage is of cargo`
    AND k's `the arbitration is to take place within one of the jurisdictions referred to in the first paragraph of Article 28`

@ref "Convention, Article 32"
GIVEN k IS A `Clause Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the clause or special agreement is null and void under Article 32` IF
        k's `the clause or special agreement purports to infringe the rules of the Convention, whether by deciding the law to be applied or by altering the rules as to jurisdiction`
    AND k's `the clause or agreement was entered into before the damage occurred`
    AND NOT `an arbitration clause is allowed by Article 32` k

§§ `Article 33. The carrier's freedom to refuse and to make regulations`

-- 33: nothing in the Convention prevents the carrier from refusing to enter into a contract of
-- carriage or from making regulations that do not conflict with it.  In the Third Schedule
-- that is "except as provided in paragraph (3) of Article 5": the carrier may not refuse
-- cargo because the other means of preserving the record cannot be used at transit or
-- destination.

@ref "Convention, Article 33"
GIVEN c IS A Convention
      `the carrier refuses because the other means of preserving the record cannot be used at transit or destination` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the carrier may refuse to enter into the contract of carriage` IF
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `the Warsaw Convention` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` THEN NOT `the carrier refuses because the other means of preserving the record cannot be used at transit or destination`

@ref "Convention, Article 33"
GIVEN `the regulation conflicts with the provisions of the Convention` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the carrier may make the regulation` IF
    NOT `the regulation conflicts with the provisions of the Convention`

§§ `Article 35. Days`

@ref "Convention, Article 35"
`the expression "days" means current days and not working days` MEANS TRUE

§§ `Articles 36 to 41. Formalities`

-- 36 (the Convention is drawn up in French in one copy deposited in the archives of the
-- Ministry for Foreign Affairs of Poland) and 37(1) and (3), 38(1) and (2), 39(1), 40, 40A(2) and
-- 41 (ratification and its notification, openness to accession, the manner of denunciation,
-- colonies and territories, the meaning of "territory", a request for a new conference, and the
-- date of signature) allocate duties among States and the depositary, and give powers that no
-- fact of a carriage can satisfy or fail: inert.  The dates that follow from Articles 37(2),
-- 38(3) and 39(2) are encoded below.

-- 37(2): as soon as five High Contracting Parties have ratified, the Convention comes into
-- force between them on the ninetieth day after the deposit of the fifth ratification, and
-- thereafter between them and a party who deposits, on the ninetieth day after that deposit.

@ref "Convention, Article 37(2)"
GIVEN t IS A `Treaty Facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the date the Convention comes into force between the first five High Contracting Parties` MEANS
    IF t's `the number of instruments of ratification deposited by that date` AT LEAST 5
    THEN JUST (t's `the date the fifth instrument of ratification was deposited` PLUS 90)
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref "Convention, Article 37(2)"
GIVEN t IS A `Treaty Facts`
GIVETH A DATE
`the date the Convention comes into force for a State that later deposits its ratification` MEANS
    t's `the date the instrument of ratification of the State is deposited` PLUS 90

@ref "Convention, Article 38(3)"
GIVEN t IS A `Treaty Facts`
GIVETH A DATE
`the date the accession takes effect` MEANS
    t's `the date the notification of accession is made` PLUS 90

@ref "Convention, Article 39(2)"
GIVEN t IS A `Treaty Facts`
GIVETH A DATE
`the date the denunciation takes effect` MEANS
    `add months` (t's `the date the notification of denunciation is made`) 6

-- 40A(1) (First and Third Schedules): in Article 37(2) and Article 40(1), "High Contracting
-- Party" means State; elsewhere it means a State whose ratification or adherence has become
-- effective and whose denunciation has not.  The Second Schedule has no Article 40A.

@ref "Convention, Article 40A(1)"
GIVEN c IS A Convention
      t IS A `Treaty Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the State is a High Contracting Party` IF
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `the Warsaw Convention` THEN REFUSE "the Warsaw Convention (Second Schedule) has no Article 40A defining a High Contracting Party"
    WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` THEN
            t's `the State's ratification or adherence has become effective`
        AND NOT t's `the State's denunciation has become effective`
    WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` THEN
            t's `the State's ratification or adherence has become effective`
        AND NOT t's `the State's denunciation has become effective`

-- The Additional Protocol: the High Contracting Parties reserve the right to declare, at
-- ratification or accession, that Article 2(1) does not apply to international carriage
-- performed directly by the State, its colonies, protectorates or mandated territories or any
-- other territory under its sovereignty, suzerainty or authority.  The declaration is a
-- fact (`the State has availed itself of the Additional Protocol`) in `Carriage Facts` and
-- `State Facts`, and its effect is in `the Convention applies to the carriage`.
